INT. NIGHT BUS, MIDWEST HIGHWAY - NIGHT

Half-lit aisle. Rows of sleeping strangers. The engine drones like a long exhale. Rain streaks the windows.

CELESTE ARMITAGE-NOLAN (30s, red scarf, paperback open on her knee) sits halfway back. Across the aisle, DOMINIC "DOM" ACHEBE (30s, rumpled suit, cold coffee) has been staring at her book for twenty minutes. He finally leans over.

DOM
Is it any good?

CELESTE
It's a murder mystery.

DOM
Does everyone die?

CELESTE
Mostly.

DOM
Sounds restful.

She laughs, quietly, despite herself. The bus hits a pothole and the whole cabin lurches. Her book slides to the floor. Dom retrieves it and hands it back. Their fingers touch.

DRIVER (V.O.)
(over intercom, crackling)
Folks, we're pulling into Dubuque for a ten-minute break. Stretch your legs. Don't wander.

CELESTE
(to the cabin, dry)
Don't wander, he says.

DOM
(to himself)
Where would I go?

He stands. The bus brakes hiss. Celeste rises too, and they collide in the narrow aisle.

CELESTE
Sorry.

DOM
No, I'm sorry.

CELESTE
I'm Celeste.

DOM
Dom.

They shake hands, lingering.

DRIVER (V.O.)
(over intercom)
Anybody traveling to Chicago, I'll be holding the bus for exactly ten minutes. Not eleven.

DOM
Chicago.

CELESTE
Me too.

He looks at her, hope in his face.

DOM
Then I guess we have eleven hours.

She picks up her book.

CELESTE
Then you'd better tell me who did it.
